A||||10||Cheever2||Making list of all major 2001 events (North America)||||1||
Z||000000||Cheever2||11-11-2000||10:19 PM||||If somebody already has such a list I haven't seen it.  If you have tried to do it by looking up the events calendars of all the clubs' websites, then you know what a pain that can be.  I haven't tried to contact Phil (FOCOA) cause I understand he's otherwise occupied right now.  So I went to the site of my local club, Lone Star, and hit the links in the club directory.  The following is what I found.  <B>Please inform me of additions and corrections</B>, email chodges1@houston.rr.com and put "Fiero events 2001" or something like it in the subject line.<P>First, there are 3 events for which I could not find dates:<BR>-Turkey Rod Run, at Daytona Int'l Speedway<BR>-National Fiero Show, at Jeffersonville Indiana<BR>-Great Pumpkin Run, somewhere in Alabama<P>There are 3 events with general time frame but exact dates unknown to me:<BR>-Run For The Hills, in North Carolina, end of Sept, beginning of Oct<BR>-Southwest Regional Fiero Fest, in Norman Oklahoma, sometime in May<BR>-Ed Parks' Swap Meet, at Toney Alabama, last weekend of April (do I assume for 2001 it's the 28th & 29th?)<P>Here are the others that I was able to find:<BR>-March 23-25, Florida Fiero Weekend, at Daytona Beach Florida<BR>-May 19, Fieros At Carlisle, at Carlisle Pennsylvania<BR>-May 31 - June 3, Dells Run 2001 A Fiero Odyssey, at Chula Vista Resort, Wisconsin<BR>-June 8-10, Pontiac Southern Nationals, in Dallas Texas<BR>-July 13-15, Michigan Fiero Festival, in Frankenmuth Michigan<BR>-July 13-15, Western Regional Fiero Fest, in San Leandro California<BR>-Aug 2-5, FOCOA Festival, in Williamsburg Virginia<BR>-Sept 9, FieroRama, in Oakbrook Illinois<P>Now, I would be happy to add events of lesser significance, but of course not the monthly club meetings.  Also feel free to mention events which are non-Fiero but INCLUDE Fieros.  Events in other countries too, just provide all information possible.  <P>I wouldn't think of trying to post it here again, so I'll just email it to anyone who requests it.<P>Again, if I'm reinventing the wheel, that's okay cause I have lots of time on my hands (unless I get that other job).  Shame on you, webmasters, for letting your sites get so sadly out of date.  Please remember you are representing all Fiero owners in your area.  If you are going to commit yourself to doing that, then do it right.<P>I would put this on a site if I had one.  Maybe someone with a respectable site will volunteer.<P>Thanks<P><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||87ECO5||11-13-2000||08:06 AM||||Chuck:  you forgot to mention all of the <B>IndyOhio Fieros</B> stuff for next year!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||Phil||11-13-2000||08:48 AM||||I believe the Jeffersonville IN "National Fiero Show" was last years FOCOA show. Cliff used to have an upcoming events page but I think that petered out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||11-14-2000||02:26 AM||||Phil is right about that show and he (and I) should know - we were there - great to meet you Phil!! -- and........I will confirm the July 13-15 Western Regional show as the 2001 San Francisco Bay Area Fiero Fest in San Leandro - reservations may be made by visiting our web site  <A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> <P>------------------<BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                             <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000004||wkayl||11-14-2000||08:27 AM||||Great topic.  I have to have all of my vacation for the year scheduled by the second week in Jan.  I would like to make at least one major event.  Maybe someone has a web page to post them on so we could bookmark it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever2||11-14-2000||08:30 PM||||Information noted, regarding Jeffersonville (Williamsburg VA next year).  <BR>Have not received any additions or corrections by email.  <BR>I'm going to add contacts to my list.  Let me know of any other names, numbers, websites, etc. to go to for more information.<BR>This is a short list.  Feel free to inform me of those local and non-Fiero events.  We won't know a whole year in advance about everything everywhere, but when you know let me know, especially if it is annual or periodic.  Let's fill up those PFF Calendars!<BR>I won't post the list again here, but just ask and I'll send you what I have (as a simple text email).<p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 11-14-2000).]||||reg||1
